{
    "type": "game",
    "name": "Minimalist Sudoku",
    "steam_appid": 3397830,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "controller_support": "full",
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sudoku originated from the Latin square studied by Swiss mathematician Euler and others in the early 18th century, and this game, &quot;Minimalist Sudoku,&quot; is likely the best Sudoku game you can find for seamless controller play.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sudoku initially was a number-filling game that used paper and pencil for calculations. Players need to deduce the numbers for all remaining empty cells on a 9\u00d79 grid based on the given numbers, ensuring that each row, each column, and each of the nine 3\u00d73 subgrids contain all digits from 1 to 9 without repetition.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Game Features:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Supports standard Sudoku and Killer Sudoku.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Perfectly supports controller play, allowing for two-player cooperative fun.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Launches with over 100 challenging puzzles, with more levels to be updated later.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Supports Steam cloud saves, instantly recording players' star-level challenge achievements.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Allows importing custom Sudoku puzzle libraries, automatically saving them to cloud storage for unlimited, anytime, anywhere enjoyment of any Sudoku puzzle.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Permits mid-game exits, fully saving the intermediate gameplay state.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Minimalist gameplay interface with various user-friendly icon prompts.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Affordable price.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >5 lively and elegant ambient music tracks.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Ideal for playing on TVs, with the best handheld experience.</p></li></ul>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sudoku originated from the Latin square studied by Swiss mathematician Euler and others in the early 18th century, and this game, &quot;Minimalist Sudoku,&quot; is likely the best Sudoku game you can find for seamless controller play.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sudoku initially was a number-filling game that used paper and pencil for calculations. Players need to deduce the numbers for all remaining empty cells on a 9\u00d79 grid based on the given numbers, ensuring that each row, each column, and each of the nine 3\u00d73 subgrids contain all digits from 1 to 9 without repetition.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Game Features:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Supports standard Sudoku and Killer Sudoku.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Perfectly supports controller play, allowing for two-player cooperative fun.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Launches with over 100 challenging puzzles, with more levels to be updated later.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Supports Steam cloud saves, instantly recording players' star-level challenge achievements.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Allows importing custom Sudoku puzzle libraries, automatically saving them to cloud storage for unlimited, anytime, anywhere enjoyment of any Sudoku puzzle.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Permits mid-game exits, fully saving the intermediate gameplay state.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Minimalist gameplay interface with various user-friendly icon prompts.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Affordable price.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >5 lively and elegant ambient music tracks.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Ideal for playing on TVs, with the best handheld experience.</p></li></ul>",
    "short_description": "A customizable Sudoku game that allows you to enjoy the joy of solving puzzles alone, as well as the fun of collaborating with others.",
    "supported_languages": "English, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, French, Italian, German, Spanish - Spain, Russian, Japanese, Korean",
